  <h2>What shoppers actually browse</h2>
  <h3>Cardholders &amp; small leather (Goyard, Celine, Chanel)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Goyard</strong>, <strong>Celine</strong>, and <strong>Chanel</strong> cardholders dominate our snapshot—compact SKUs that ship cheaply in ¥ but need macro QC on emboss depth and logo alignment.
    Compare stitching rhythm in warehouse stills; seller studio lighting hides grain mismatch.
  </p>
  <h3>Designer accents (Dior, Gucci, Burberry)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Dior</strong> and <strong>Gucci</strong> rows mix card cases with belt-adjacent listings; <strong>Burberry</strong> check patterns recur.
    These SKUs still trigger <a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded shipping</a> scrutiny—confirm route eligibility before you build an accessories-only cart.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for jewelry &amp; watch rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Stamp fonts:</strong> interior logo spacing, heat-stamp clarity, serial-style numbers if shown.</li>
    <li><strong>Hardware:</strong> clasp weight, buckle engravings, zipper pulls on wallet hybrids.</li>
    <li><strong>Pattern alignment:</strong> monogram continuity across seams and corners.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch-specific (if applicable):</strong> dial printing, crown branding, bracelet link finish.</li>
    <li><strong>Included packaging:</strong> verify dust bags or boxes if listing promises them.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Deep-read <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">warehouse QC</a> and <a href="/blog/kakobuy-4k-qc-video-inspection-guide/">4K video</a> for curved leather panels.
  </p>

